<article class="env-remark" id="09SS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09SS">Remark <span data-tag="09SS">22.37.3</span>.</a> In Lemma <a href="/tag/09S7" data-tag="09S7">22.37.2</a> we can replace condition (2) by the condition that $N$ is a classical generator for $D_{compact}(B, d)$, see Derived Categories, Proposition <a href="/tag/09SR" data-tag="09SR">13.37.6</a>. Moreover, if we knew that $R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (N, B)$ is a compact object of $D(A, \text{d})$, then it suffices to check that $N$ is a weak generator for $D_{compact}(B, \text{d})$. We omit the proof; we will add it here if we ever need it in the Stacks project. </p>
</article>